Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.bbq-predictor.server-only>
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
# The SQLite driver is loaded at run time, so it appears in no ELF
# header and dpkg-shlibdeps cannot see it. Without this the archive
# cannot be opened at all.
         libqt6sql6-sqlite
Description: weather applet and forecast-verification archive
 A Qt Widgets applet that draws high-resolution temperature and rain
 graphs from several providers at once, and answers whether an afternoon
 is worth lighting a fire for.
 .
 It keeps a permanent archive of what was observed and what was
 forecast, scores each provider against the measurements as they arrive,
 and corrects later forecasts by the bias it has measured.

Package: bbq-predictor-server
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
# The publisher's archive, for the reason the applet's line gives.
         libqt6sql6-sqlite,
# Every provider is HTTPS, and Qt's network library only recommends the
# trust store: a bare trixie with only this package failed every
# handshake with "the issuer certificate ... could not be found"
# (project.md sec 15.13).
         ca-certificates
# Where systemd is not running, cron runs the round instead of the timer.
Recommends: cron | cron-daemon
# The scheduled round, its configuration and its account were the
# applet's package's until 0.1.0-2 (project.md sec 15.13).
Breaks: bbq-predictor (<< 0.1.0-2)
Replaces: bbq-predictor (<< 0.1.0-2)
Description: server for the bbq-predictor weather archive
 The publisher, bbq-predictor-publish, fetches every band on a five-minute
 timer (or cron where systemd is not running) and writes the station's
 signed files. It uses Qt's core, network and SQL libraries and nothing
 that draws, so a server needs no display and no desktop libraries.
 .
 The daemon, bbq-predictor-serve, answers bbq-predictor clients from those
 files: a fixed 48-byte request, and a prebuilt file held in memory in
 reply. There is no HTTP and no TLS; every file is signed with Ed25519 and
 checked by the applet, and the daemon never holds the signing key.
 .
 It binds its ports as root, then chroots into the published tree as an
 account of its own. The init script runs under sysvinit and OpenRC, and
 the service is not started on install: configure the ports in
 /etc/default/bbq-predictor-serve, then start it.
